abstract: >-
  MarxKapital is an open-source Julia package for the mathematical
  modeling of Marxian value theory: capital accumulation, the tendency
  of the rate of profit, the transformation of labor values into prices
  of production, and the sectoral dynamics of expanded reproduction.
  Beyond the classical two-department and generalized N-department
  reproduction schemes, it implements three coupling mechanisms for
  sectoral accumulation through the technical matrix A -- capital
  mobility, an aggregate realization-pressure heuristic, and an exact
  per-sector quantity-rationing scheme solved by fixed-point iteration
  -- and a live, reproducible empirical calibration pipeline drawing
  directly from official European statistical sources (Eurostat and
  AMECO, via their SDMX REST APIs). An accompanying academic paper
  (paper/main.tex) applies the pipeline to Portugal.
